<title>LEBANON: Lebanon issues money supply statistics.</title>
<headline>Lebanon issues money supply statistics.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank released on Monday latest statistics on money supply during the month of September (bln of Lebanese pounds at end of period):</p>
<p>				  M1	   M2	 M3	M4</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>    Jan			1516	10092     23162    N/A</p>
<p>    April		    1713	10490     24204    N/A</p>
<p>    July		     1763	11719     25739   29696</p>
<p>    Aug			1771	11986     26162   30309</p>
<p>    Sept		     1816	12386     26524   30746</p>
<p>1995</p>
<p>    July		     1441	 8597     21945   24008</p>
<p>    Sept		     1651	 8120     22338   24581</p>
<p>    Dec			1561	 9663     22883   26233</p>
<p>1994</p>
<p>    Dec			1437	 8587     19651   21549</p>
<p>1993</p>
<p>    Dec			1143	 5309     15678    N/A</p>
<p>The Bank defined the aggregates as follows:</p>
<p>M1 -- Currency in circulation + Demand deposits</p>
<p>M2 -- M1 + Other deposits in Lebanese pounds</p>
<p>M3 -- M2 + Deposits in F.X.</p>
<p>M4 -- M3 + Treasury bills held by the non-banking system</p>
<p>($1 = 1,558.5 Lebanese pounds in September)</p>
